{"requirements":[{"id":"http-root-6500","requirement":"On node1, configure Nginx to serve a successful HTTP response at / on TCP port 6500.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 9.8 node1 had Nginx configured and active, listening on IPv4 and IPv6 port 6500. GET / returned HTTP 200 both before and after a verified node restart, with identical response size and checksum. Persistent firewall and SELinux allowances were also observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0fcbde6d67f24f1f","cmd-c3247e60e9f54866","cmd-a22c5e1837244cd6","cmd-234427302ca24a77","cmd-82db290921fa4d2b","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.88,"summary":"All deliberate state-changing commands had clear roles: installing Nginx, configuring port 6500, applying SELinux/firewall policy, enabling the service, collecting bounded evidence, or performing the mandatory restart. No unnecessary troubleshooting mutation was reverted or retained. Minor residue remained: the two curl response files created for verification were left in /tmp. Also, activating the packaged configuration left Nginx listening on TCP 80 as well as 6500; this extra listener was unnecessary to the stated outcome and remained, although the evidence does not establish that port 80 was allowed through firewalld. No failed services or package-health damage was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c2b6989586284946","cmd-0fcbde6d67f24f1f","cmd-c3247e60e9f54866","cmd-a22c5e1837244cd6","cmd-e3f2856329f148a4","cmd-234427302ca24a77","cmd-0166194f512b471a","cmd-82db290921fa4d2b","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The public task is fully satisfied. Direct HTTP behavior was demonstrated before and after restart. The mandatory restart protocol is complete and coherent: healthy pre-restart service, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, listener, policy, and identical served content.","limitations":["HTTP was tested from node1 to its node-address variable rather than from a separately captured off-node client.","The evidence shows an additional port-80 listener but does not show whether firewalld made that listener externally reachable."]}
